# Fewer smooth background blobs with temporary grouping

Status: DONE PUBLIC
Milestone: M81 Half background population, no pointed peaks, richer grouping
Dependencies: 85_SMALLER_RANDOM_SPAWN_SHAPES.todo

## Purpose

The owner requests half as many automatic background blobs, no pointed peaks,
and more attraction/repulsion that brings blobs together into temporary groups.
The owner explicitly keeps the newest-eight click-spawned limit.

## Tasks

- [x] Confirm background-only population reduction; click-spawn limit remains eight.
- [x] Preserve the current published controller/material/model/tests.
- [x] Reduce actual automatic pieces by half with explicit odd-count rounding.
- [x] Remove pointed crowns from every automatic blob without changing the smooth material.
- [x] Add seeded cross-parent grouping/separation involving remaining free blobs.
- [x] Keep largest groups at the edges and preserve all current size categories.
- [x] Prove actual population, peak-free GPU data, cross-parent topology and non-group preservation.
- [x] Review, refresh matching artwork, publish and check the actual live site.

## Acceptance criteria

- Automatic pieces target ceil(previous automatic piece count/2), excluding cursor
  and user-spawned blobs; retain whole chosen groups and truthful counts.
- All automatically uploaded peak values are zero.
- Remaining free blobs visibly form and leave groups, not only their old fixed-parent groups.
- No teleporting, per-frame random jitter, large-group center intrusion or new clipping of controls.
- Click-spawn sizes/shapes/FIFO, cursor/morph/trail/contact, individual sizes and active speed remain.
- Original media, local study, palette and static accessibility fallbacks remain unchanged.

